{"id":"p13-l14","minutes":45,"summary":"The Nyquist criterion decides closed-loop stability from the open-loop frequency response alone, by counting how many times the plot of L around the whole right half-plane contour encircles the point minus one, and it handles unstable plants and integrators that Bode-based margins cannot. You derive it from the argument principle, implement an adaptive contour with indentations around imaginary-axis poles, and test that N = Z minus P predicts stability correctly in 11 cases checked against the closed-loop roots.","html":"<h2 id=\"the-argument-principle\">The argument principle</h2>\n<p>Trace a closed contour in the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span></span></span></span>-plane clockwise. For a rational function <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, the image <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> encircles the origin clockwise</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>times, where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span> count the zeros and poles of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span></span></span></span> inside the contour.</p>\n<h2 id=\"applying-it-to-feedback\">Applying it to feedback</h2>\n<p>Take <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span>. Its zeros are the closed-loop poles; its poles are the open-loop poles. Choose the <strong>Nyquist contour</strong>: up the imaginary axis and round a huge semicircle enclosing the right half-plane. Encircling the origin by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> is the same as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> encircling <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>. So</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span> is the number of open-loop right-half-plane poles and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> the clockwise encirclements of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0572em;\">j</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>. Stable means <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>: an open-loop stable plant (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>) must not encircle <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>; an unstable one must encircle it counter-clockwise <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span></span></span></span> times.</p>\n<p><strong>Poles on the imaginary axis</strong> (integrators, undamped pairs) sit on the contour. Detour round them on tiny semicircles to the right; there <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> swings round a huge arc, which is where most hand-drawn plots go wrong.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"nyquistplot\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>The Nyquist plot of a loop with an integrator and the critical point −1. Raise the gain until the plot wraps around −1: the count of encirclements switches and the closed loop goes unstable.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.2963em;vertical-align:-0.936em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span>: one open-loop RHP pole, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>At <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span>. As <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> from below; the plot is a loop through <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span> the plot crosses the real axis at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1.5</span></span></span></span>, left of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, and circles <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> once counter-clockwise: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>. Stable: the characteristic polynomial <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> confirms it.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> it crosses at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span></span></span></span> and doesn’t encircle <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>. Unstable (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> has a root at 0.62).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">nyquist.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">winding</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">F, path, t0=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, t1=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, depth=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;total change of arg F(path(t)) over [t0, t1], subdividing until each step is small&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    a, b = F(path(t0)), F(path(t1))\n    d = np.angle(b / a)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> (<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(d) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.2</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> depth &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> depth &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span>:\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> d\n    tm = (t0 + t1) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> winding(F, path, t0, tm, depth + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) + winding(F, path, tm, t1, depth + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">axis_pt</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b, t</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;frequency between a and b, spaced like asinh so that low frequencies get fine steps&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.sinh(np.arcsinh(a) + (np.arcsinh(b) - np.arcsinh(a)) * t)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">nyquist_N</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">num, den, R=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e4</span>, eps=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-4</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;clockwise encirclements of -1 by L = num/den along the indented Nyquist contour&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    L = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> s: np.polyval(num, s) / np.polyval(den, s)\n    F = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> s: <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + L(s)\n    axis = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sorted</span>({<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(r.imag, <span class=\"hljs-number\">9</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> r <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> np.roots(den) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(r.real) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>})\n    pieces, w0 = [], -R\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> wp <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> axis:                                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># straight up the axis, small right detours at each pole</span>\n        pieces.append(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> t, a=w0, b=wp - eps: <span class=\"hljs-number\">1j</span> * axis_pt(a, b, t))\n        pieces.append(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> t, c=wp: <span class=\"hljs-number\">1j</span> * c + eps * np.exp(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1j</span> * (-np.pi / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> + np.pi * t)))\n        w0 = wp + eps\n    pieces.append(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> t, a=w0: <span class=\"hljs-number\">1j</span> * axis_pt(a, R, t))\n    pieces.append(<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> t: R * np.exp(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1j</span> * (np.pi / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> - np.pi * t)))     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># big arc, clockwise</span>\n    total = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(winding(F, p) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> p <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> pieces)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> -<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(total / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi)))               <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># counter-clockwise arg change -&gt; clockwise count</span>\n\nCASES = [   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># (description, numerator, denominator)</span>\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;4/(s+1)^3&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>], np.poly([-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;10/(s+1)^3&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>], np.poly([-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;3/(s(s+1)(s+2))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;8/(s(s+1)(s+2))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;3/((s-1)(s+2))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;1/((s-1)(s+2))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;10(s+1)/(s^2(s+5))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;1/(s^2(s+1))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;4(s+2)/((s-1)(s+5))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;2(s+2)/((s-1)(s+5))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>], np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>])),\n    (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;1/((s^2+4)(s+1))&quot;</span>, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], np.real(np.poly([<span class=\"hljs-number\">2j</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2j</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]))),\n]\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_predicts_stability</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> name, num, den <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> CASES:\n        num, den = np.array(num, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">float</span>), np.array(den, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">float</span>)\n        N = nyquist_N(num, den)\n        P = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(np.roots(den).real &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>))\n        Z = N + P\n        cl = np.roots(np.polyadd(den, num))\n        Z_true = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(cl.real &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-9</span>))\n        <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{name:22s}</span>: P = <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{P}</span>, N = <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{N:+d}</span> -&gt; Z = <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{Z}</span> (<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;stable&#x27;</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> Z == <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;unstable&#x27;</span>}</span>); closed-loop roots give <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{Z_true}</span>&quot;</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> Z == Z_true\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(CASES)}</span> cases predicted correctly&quot;</span>)\n\ntest_predicts_stability()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why is a loop with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span> unstable for every positive gain?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The double integrator sends the indentation’s image round a full 360° arc at infinite radius, and with the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> lag the plot then passes on the wrong side of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, giving <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span> for any <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span>. Equivalently, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span></span></span></span> has a zero <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span></span></span></span> coefficient, so it fails Routh’s necessary condition. A zero (lead) is needed to stabilise it, as in the case <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why can’t you read stability of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3/</span><span class=\"mopen\">((</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span> from a Bode phase margin?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Margins assume the open loop is stable (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>), so that “no encirclement” means stable. Here <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">P</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> and stability requires one counter-clockwise encirclement, which shows up on the Nyquist plot but has no clean meaning on a Bode plot.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p13-l14\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"the-argument-principle","title":"The argument principle"},{"id":"applying-it-to-feedback","title":"Applying it to feedback"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p13-l14-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Closed-loop RHP poles if P = 1 and the plot encircles −1 once clockwise?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Z = N + P.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Encirclements needed for stability when P = 2 (counting clockwise as positive)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two counter-clockwise.</p>\n","answer":-2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Where does L = K/((s − 1)(s + 2)) cross the negative real axis at ω = 0 for K = 3?</p>\n","explain":"<p>L(0) = −K/2.</p>\n","answer":-1.5,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Smallest K that stabilises K/((s − 1)(s + 2))?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The constant term K − 2 must be positive.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l14-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The zeros of 1 + L(s) are…</p>\n","explain":"<p>1 + L = (D + N)/D.</p>\n","options":["the closed-loop poles","the open-loop zeros","the open-loop poles","always stable"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l14-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Why indent the contour around poles on the imaginary axis?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The detour maps to a large arc.</p>\n","options":["L is infinite there, so the contour must avoid them","to make the plot symmetric","to count zeros","to remove the integrator"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"nyquist.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ndef winding(F, path, t0=0.0, t1=1.0, depth=0):\n    \"\"\"total change of arg F(path(t)) over [t0, t1], subdividing until each step is small\"\"\"\n    a, b = F(path(t0)), F(path(t1))\n    d = np.angle(b / a)\n    if (abs(d) < 0.2 or depth > 50) and depth > 6:\n        return d\n    tm = (t0 + t1) / 2\n    return winding(F, path, t0, tm, depth + 1) + winding(F, path, tm, t1, depth + 1)\n\ndef axis_pt(a, b, t):\n    \"\"\"frequency between a and b, spaced like asinh so that low frequencies get fine steps\"\"\"\n    return np.sinh(np.arcsinh(a) + (np.arcsinh(b) - np.arcsinh(a)) * t)\n\ndef nyquist_N(num, den, R=1e4, eps=1e-4):\n    \"\"\"clockwise encirclements of -1 by L = num/den along the indented Nyquist contour\"\"\"\n    L = lambda s: np.polyval(num, s) / np.polyval(den, s)\n    F = lambda s: 1 + L(s)\n    axis = sorted({round(r.imag, 9) for r in np.roots(den) if abs(r.real) < 1e-9})\n    pieces, w0 = [], -R\n    for wp in axis:                                       # straight up the axis, small right detours at each pole\n        pieces.append(lambda t, a=w0, b=wp - eps: 1j * axis_pt(a, b, t))\n        pieces.append(lambda t, c=wp: 1j * c + eps * np.exp(1j * (-np.pi / 2 + np.pi * t)))\n        w0 = wp + eps\n    pieces.append(lambda t, a=w0: 1j * axis_pt(a, R, t))\n    pieces.append(lambda t: R * np.exp(1j * (np.pi / 2 - np.pi * t)))     # big arc, clockwise\n    total = sum(winding(F, p) for p in pieces)\n    return -int(round(total / (2 * np.pi)))               # counter-clockwise arg change -> clockwise count\n\nCASES = [   # (description, numerator, denominator)\n    (\"4/(s+1)^3\", [4], np.poly([-1, -1, -1])),\n    (\"10/(s+1)^3\", [10], np.poly([-1, -1, -1])),\n    (\"3/(s(s+1)(s+2))\", [3], np.poly([0, -1, -2])),\n    (\"8/(s(s+1)(s+2))\", [8], np.poly([0, -1, -2])),\n    (\"3/((s-1)(s+2))\", [3], np.poly([1, -2])),\n    (\"1/((s-1)(s+2))\", [1], np.poly([1, -2])),\n    (\"10(s+1)/(s^2(s+5))\", [10, 10], np.poly([0, 0, -5])),\n    (\"1/(s^2(s+1))\", [1], np.poly([0, 0, -1])),\n    (\"4(s+2)/((s-1)(s+5))\", [4, 8], np.poly([1, -5])),\n    (\"2(s+2)/((s-1)(s+5))\", [2, 4], np.poly([1, -5])),\n    (\"1/((s^2+4)(s+1))\", [1], np.real(np.poly([2j, -2j, -1]))),\n]\n\ndef test_predicts_stability():\n    for name, num, den in CASES:\n        num, den = np.array(num, float), np.array(den, float)\n        N = nyquist_N(num, den)\n        P = int(np.sum(np.roots(den).real > 1e-9))\n        Z = N + P\n        cl = np.roots(np.polyadd(den, num))\n        Z_true = int(np.sum(cl.real > 1e-9))\n        print(f\"{name:22s}: P = {P}, N = {N:+d} -> Z = {Z} ({'stable' if Z == 0 else 'unstable'}); closed-loop roots give {Z_true}\")\n        assert Z == Z_true\n    print(f\"{len(CASES)} cases predicted correctly\")\n\ntest_predicts_stability()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}